{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VTEvixu5DtS4M6XpyGWH8m","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md:103:- req-seed: `testdata/seed.json` holds the two seed links (`zurdo` → `https://github.com/ElOrlis/zurdo`, `carol` → `https://github.com/ElOrlis/carol`), and the dev server serves them.\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md-104-- req-redirect: the live dev server redirects `/zurdo` with a 302 to the zurdo repository.\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md-105-- req-clean: `gofmt -l .`, `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...` are clean, with the pre-authored tests included.\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md-106-\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md-107-### Description\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md-108-\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md-109-Add a `serve` subcommand to `cmd/shortlink`. Use the `flag` package for its\n--\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md:117:`{\"slug\",\"url\"}` objects) holding the two seed links listed under req-seed.\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md-118-\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md-119-The live checks run against the dev server that `scripts/devserver.sh` serves\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md-120-from the newest tree on `http://127.0.0.1:8787`. Do not start another server\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md-121-on that port, and do not modify `scripts/devserver.sh`.\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md-122-\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md-123-### Acceptance Criteria\n--\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md:127:- [ ] the live list carries the zurdo seed link [http: GET http://127.0.0.1:8787/api/links -> 200 contains \"\\\"slug\\\":\\\"zurdo\\\"\"] [proves: req-seed]\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md:128:- [ ] the live server reads the carol seed link and 404s an unknown slug [http: GET http://127.0.0.1:8787/api/links/carol -> 200 contains \"https://github.com/ElOrlis/carol\"] [http: GET http://127.0.0.1:8787/api/links/nope -> 404] [proves: req-seed]\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md-129-- [ ] the live server redirects /zurdo without following it [shell: curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code} %{redirect_url}\\n' http://127.0.0.1:8787/zurdo | grep -qx '302 https://github.com/ElOrlis/zurdo'] [proves: req-redirect]\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md-130-- [ ] the tree is gofmt-clean, vets clean and the full suite passes with pre-authored tests included [shell: test -z \"$(gofmt -l .)\" && go vet ./... && go vet -tags=preauthored ./... && go test -tags=preauthored -count=1 ./...] [proves: req-clean]\n# Scope: Shortlink\n\n## Destination\n\nShortlink is a small Go URL shortener, built phase by phase by Zurdo and driven by Carol: `shortlink serve` is an HTTP API that stores and redirects links, and `shortlink add/list/resolve/stats` is a CLI client for it.\n\nDone when every phase is `done`, each having gone from `carol:accepted` on its proposal to `carol:reported` on its epic, with humans acting only at the gates.\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Domain:** a URL shortener: links, slugs, redirects and click counts. One binary; `serve` is the API and every other subcommand is a client.\n- **Design record:** [design/shortlink.md](design/shortlink.md) — one section per phase, which `carol specify` hands to `zurdo scaffold`.\n- **Standing preferences:** Go 1.22 standard library only; `gofmt` and `go vet` clean; table-driven tests with `httptest`. `[http:]` criteria target the dev server on `127.0.0.1:8787` (`scripts/devserver.sh`), which must be running while a phase runs.\n\n## Decisions so far\n\n- Initiative scoped (maintainer, 2026-10-19). Three phases, each with its own section in [the design record](design/shortlink.md): the HTTP API first, the CLI client on top of it, then click stats across both. Every phase carries a `Design` cell so Carol can specify it without a hand-authored PRD.\n- `[http:]` criteria run against a live dev server (2026-10-19). zurdo's PRD grammar has no setup step, so `scripts/devserver.sh` rebuilds and restarts `shortlink serve` on every `.go` change and follows the newest `.carol/worktrees/<phase>`, with fresh `testdata/seed.json` data on each restart.\n\n## Phases\n\n| Phase | Title | PRD | Status | Depends on | Design |\n|-------|-------|-----|--------|------------|--------|\n| phase-01 | Link store and HTTP API | docs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md | running | | design/shortlink.md#Phase 1 — link store and HTTP API |\n| phase-02 | CLI client | | ready | phase-01 | design/shortlink.md#Phase 2 — CLI client |\n| phase-03 | Click stats | | ready | phase-02 | design/shortlink.md#Phase 3 — click stats |\n\n## Not yet specified\n\n- Whether a later phase adds a `[manual]` criterion to show `zurdo review --sign-off` (design record open question 1).\n- Link expiry and deletion (`DELETE /api/links/{slug}`).\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Authentication and users — they add no new kind of criterion to the demo.\n- A database — a JSON file keeps every run hermetic.\n- A web UI — `[http:]` checks status codes and bodies; HTML adds nothing to show.\nmodule github.com/BotJakeDemo/shortlink\n\ngo 1.22","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"61af20a2-088b-4744-bc48-6ec774f6c578","uuid":"226f7329-ad4b-4318-adaf-584a98626a29","timestamp":"2026-10-19T08:33:03.957Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"docs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md:103:- req-seed: `testdata/seed.json` holds the two seed links (`zurdo` → `https://github.com/ElOrlis/zurdo`, `carol` → `https://github.com/ElOrlis/carol`), and the dev server serves them.\ndocs/shortlink/prds/prd-01-link-store-and-http-api.md-104-- req-redirect: the live dev server redi